 "about_text": "The Broad is a contemporary art museum on Grand Avenue in downtown Los Angeles, founded in 2015 by philanthropists Eli and Edythe Broad as a gift to the city. Designed by Diller Scofidio + Renfro with Gensler, its 120,000-square-foot 'veil-and-vault' building offers free general admission and houses over 2,000 postwar and contemporary works by nearly 200 artists, including Basquiat, Warhol, Koons, Kusama, Ruscha, and Kruger. The museum is also headquarters to the Broad Art Foundation's worldwide lending library, active since 1984. Under founding director Joanne Heyler, its program emphasizes rotating temporary exhibitions, monographic surveys, and public programming often centered on social justice themes, drawing over 900,000 visitors annually.",
